From 2b2d01a02d1ae8f87a5faced83de6d0e2aa824cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alvaro Figueroa <alvarof@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:38:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] espressif: add Meshnology W12

ESP32-S3R8 with 16 MB flash and 8 MB octal PSRAM, Heltec V3-style
pinout. The board ships with no UF2 bootloader.

partitions-16MB.csv matches CircuitPython's own 16 MB layout offset for
offset (ota_0 0x10000, ota_1 0x210000, uf2 0x410000, FAT 0x450000), so
a CircuitPython image for this board drops onto W12BOOT as-is.

UF2 entry is BOOT (GPIO0) pressed while the RGB LED on GPIO46 is lit
after reset: no RC network is fitted on a free GPIO, so there is no
double-reset detection. Holding BOOT through reset reaches the ROM
bootloader instead.

USB PID 0xFED2 under Espressif's VID, the same pair the CircuitPython
firmware for this board uses.

Carried by cpy-meshtastic in temp-board-patches/ until it is upstream.
---
 .../boards/meshnology_w12/board.cmake         |  2 +
 ports/espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/board.h | 80 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/sdkconfig | 12 +++
 3 files changed, 94 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ports/espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/board.cmake
 create mode 100644 ports/espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/board.h
 create mode 100644 ports/espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/sdkconfig

diff --git a/ports/espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/board.cmake b/ports/espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/board.cmake
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9bac46d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ports/espressif/boards/meshnology_w12/board.cmake
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+# Apply board specific content here
+set(IDF_TARGET "esp32s3")
